      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. like the Norwegian thing proves it's actually being done. but what i'm getting at is that it feels way more intentional than just a privacy mistake. the way the app updates and the way the sensors respond to certain movements... it feels like they're training an AI model on us in real-time to predict behavior or even emotional states based on how we walk. if a company actually had a database of millions of people's biometric 'signatures' like that, how much power would they actually have? it's basically a backdoor into our physical and mental state, isn't it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
